# Repo has GitHub secret scanning enabled
# Platform: GitHub (SDLC::Repository assets)
# CTN: github_repo_metadata
# Frameworks: KSI-SVC-ASM, KSI-MLA-LET, NIST IA-5, CMMC IA.L2-3.5.10

META
    esp_id `github-repo-secret-scanning-enabled-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `github`
    criticality `medium`

    category `asset_list`
    target_asset_type `SDLC::Repository`

    title `Repo has secret scanning enabled`
    description `Validates that the repository has GitHub secret scanning turned on. Secret scanning continuously inspects pushed content and existing history for credential patterns; without it, accidentally committed secrets go undetected and rotation lags by months.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `github,sdlc,secrets,secret-scanning,ksi-svc-asm,ksi-mla-let,nist-ia-5,cmmc-ia-l2-3.5.10`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-SVC-ASM,KSI:KSI-MLA-LET,NIST-800-53:IA-5,CMMC:IA.L2-3.5.10`
    control_objective `KSI-SVC-ASM,IA.L2-3.5.10`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`
    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `GitHub:scanset:sdlc-baseline`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `14`
    recommendation `Settings, Code security, "Secret scanning": enable. For public repos this is on by default; for private repos this requires GitHub Advanced Security or is available free on enterprise plans depending on tier.`

    component_id `comp-github-sdlc`

    impl_KSI_SVC_ASM `Secrets management for SDLC artifacts requires continuous detection of inadvertent secret disclosure in source. GitHub secret scanning matches pushed and historical content against published provider patterns (AWS keys, GitHub tokens, third-party API keys) and notifies repository admins of matches. The CTN reads the security_and_analysis.secret_scanning.status field and the policy fails when it is not "enabled".`
    impl_IA_L2_3_5_10 `Identification and authentication credentials are protected throughout their lifecycle, including detection of compromise via accidental publication to source. Secret scanning provides the continuous detection layer; remediation through immediate rotation is owned by the responsible team.`

META_END

DEF
    # Default placeholder values, overridden per-asset by PolicySetSync
    # at bind time. The VARs are pattern-fillers consumed by the template
    # OBJECT below; on bind, PolicySetSync rewrites the SET body with one
    # OBJECT per bound asset, each carrying that asset's concrete
    # owner / repo from inventory.assets.metadata.
    VAR owner string `_unbound_`
    VAR repo string `_unbound_`

    # Bound assets - managed programmatically by PolicySetSync from
    # inventory.asset_policies (status = active). Do not hand-edit;
    # the SET body is the only mutable region of this file.
    SET github_repos union
        OBJECT repo_target
            owner VAR owner
            repo VAR repo
        OBJECT_END
    SET_END

    STATE secret_scanning_on
        found boolean = true
        secret_scanning_enabled boolean = true
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN github_repo_metadata
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF secret_scanning_on
            SET_REF github_repos
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
